                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/pulls/comments/3532733101"
                }
            },
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "This array stores *function* addresses in a `void *` array (e.g. `(void *)&lua_tothread`). Converting a function pointer to an object pointer is not allowed by ISO C and is diagnosed by `-Wpedantic`; with Neovim’s `-pedantic` (and `-Werror` in CI builds) this can fail compilation.\n\nConsider switching the anchor storage to a function-pointer array (e.g. `void (*)(void)` with explicit casts) to avoid UB and toolchain-dependent diagnostics. As a minimal stopgap, suppress the specific pedantic warning for this translation unit so CI builds don’t break.",
            "commit_id": "41966211ecfd3b832f0239cfc856c0c3a0a7cfbb",
            "created_at": "2026-07-06T23:58:14Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -0,0 +1,150 @@\n+#include <lauxlib.h>\n+#include <lua.h>\n+#include <lualib.h>\n+\n+#if defined(__GNUC__)\n+# define NVIM_LUA_C_API_USED __attribute__((used))\n+#else\n+# define NVIM_LUA_C_API_USED\n+#endif\n+\n+// Keep Lua C API symbols available for dlopen()'d native modules.\n+static void *const lua_c_api_symbols[] NVIM_LUA_C_API_USED = {",
