            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This is the wrong solution. we do not use blacklists/whitelists of symbols as \"policy\" nor as a \"mechanism\".\r\n\r\n _All_ symbols which are non-`static` should be exposed out of the binary as delicious PIE. This is the behavior on GNOOO/LINUX and the task at hand is to find whatever arcane build system incantations which are necessary to match this simple sanity on windows, darwin and other supported platforms.",
